---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'What is Krillion?' }
];

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is Krillion?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Krillion is a daily online reverse-trivia browser game where players plunge into an ocean trench by answering factual prompts across 7 categories. Unlike standard trivia where popular answers win, Krillion awards depth based on rarity: the fewer players who choose your valid answer, the deeper your submarine sinks toward the 7,000-meter Hadal Abyss."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does scoring work in Krillion?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Each valid answer scores between 0m and 1,000m depth based on global frequency distribution. Across the 7 prompts of a daily dive, the maximum achievable cumulative score is 7,000 meters."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the 'Too-Clever' trap in Krillion?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The Too-Clever trap occurs when many knowledgeable players simultaneously submit the same mid-tier 'smart' answer (e.g., Caligula for Roman Emperors or Monaco for microstates), resulting in a sudden crowd penalty and stalling their depth around 2,500m–4,500m."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<Layout
  title="What is Krillion? The Viral Reverse-Trivia Deep Sea Game Explained - Krillion.si"
  description="What is Krillion? Learn how the viral ocean trench trivia game works, why common answers drown at the surface, how the 7,000m scoring system works, and how to play online."
  schema={faqSchema}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 prose prose-invert prose-cyan">
    <!-- Breadcrumb & Header -->
    <div class="not-prose mb-8 space-y-3">
      <Breadcrumb items={breadcrumbs} />
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-cyan-950/60 border border-cyan-500/30 text-cyan-400 text-xs font-bold font-mono">
        <span>EXPLAINER & ARCHITECTURE</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black text-white leading-tight">
        What is Krillion? The Reverse-Trivia Trench Diver Explained
      </h1>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-xs sm:text-sm">
        By Krillion Strategy Guild • Updated 2026 • Verified Definition & Depth Mechanics
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Quick Definition Box (Optimized for AI Engines & Google Featured Snippet) -->
    <div class="bg-abyss-card border border-cyan-500/30 rounded-3xl p-6 my-8 not-prose space-y-3 shadow-lg shadow-cyan-950/20">
      <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-cyan-400 flex items-center gap-1.5 font-mono">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-cyan-400" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 16v-4"/><path d="M12 8h.01"/></svg>
        <span>Direct Definition (Generative Engine Capsule)</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-200 leading-relaxed font-medium">
        <strong class="text-white">Krillion</strong> is a daily online reverse-trivia browser game where players navigate an abyssal trench by entering valid factual answers across 7 categories. Rather than rewarding popular facts or speed, Krillion awards <strong class="text-cyan-400">depth in meters</strong> based on <em>mathematical rarity</em>: common answers keep you stranded near the surface (0m–1,500m), while verified, low-frequency historical, geographical, and scientific answers plunge you to the <strong class="text-cyan-400">7,000-meter Hadal Abyss</strong>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>How Does the Krillion Game Work?</h2>
    <p>
      In a standard daily round of Krillion, players are presented with a series of <strong>7 category prompts</strong> spanning World History, Global Geography, Literature, Science, and Cinema.
    </p>
    <p>
      For each prompt, you have about 20 seconds to submit a single valid answer. The game's engine calculates your depth against 4 distinct strata:
    </p>

    <!-- Visual Tier Comparison Table -->
    <div class="not-prose my-8 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-xs text-left bg-abyss-card rounded-2xl border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
        <thead class="bg-white/5 uppercase text-slate-400 font-mono">
          <tr>
            <th class="p-3.5">Zone & Depth</th>
            <th class="p-3.5">Answer Type</th>
            <th class="p-3.5">Example (Prompt: Roman Emperor)</th>
            <th class="p-3.5">Why It Scores This Way</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/5 font-mono">
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-blue-400">0m - 1,500m<br /><span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 font-normal">Sunlight Surface Floater</span></td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-slate-300 font-sans">Pop-culture consensus</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-medium text-white"><em>Augustus, Julius Caesar, Nero</em></td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-slate-400 font-sans">Chosen by 60%+ of participants; excessive crowd consensus prevents diving.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-amber-400">2,500m - 4,500m<br /><span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 font-normal">Too-Clever Crowd Trap</span></td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-slate-300 font-sans">Textbook "smart" answer</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-medium text-white"><em>Caligula, Marcus Aurelius, Hadrian</em></td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-slate-400 font-sans">Intelligent players think nobody else will choose it, causing a mid-depth cluster.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-cyan-300">5,000m - 6,500m<br /><span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 font-normal">Bathyal Trench Sinker</span></td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-slate-300 font-sans">Secondary historical fact</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-medium text-white"><em>Diocletian, Probus, Majorian</em></td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-slate-400 font-sans">Genuine rarity with very few daily participants guessing it.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-cyan-400">7,000m (Max Depth)<br /><span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 font-normal">Hadal Abyss Crown 👑</span></td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-slate-300 font-sans">Ultra-niche valid archival footnote</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-medium text-white"><em>Didius Julianus, Pertinax, Gordian I</em></td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-slate-400 font-sans">Under 0.05% selection rate. Unlocks maximum depth and viral bragging rights.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Why is Krillion So Addictive?</h2>
    <p>
      Krillion turns traditional trivia on its head by introducing <strong>psychological game theory</strong>:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cognitive Second-Guessing:</strong> You can't just know a fact; you must anticipate what <em>other players know</em> and actively veer away from consensus.</li>
      <li><strong>The "Too-Clever" Agony:</strong> Getting trapped at 3,200m with an answer you thought was a genius secret creates immense drive to replay and refine your strategy.</li>
      <li><strong>Viral Daily Share Grids:</strong> Like Wordle, players share an emoji depth grid across social platforms to compare their total depth.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where Can You Play Krillion?</h2>
    <p>
      You can play instantly right here on <strong>Krillion.si</strong>:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong><a href="/daily" class="text-cyan-400 font-semibold">Daily Dive</a>:</strong> 7 official prompts updated each calendar day.</li>
      <li><strong><a href="/endless" class="text-cyan-400 font-semibold">Endless Mode</a>:</strong> Unlimited practice rounds with zero waiting periods, perfect for training your 7,000m instinct.</li>
      <li><strong><a href="/#variants" class="text-cyan-400 font-semibold">Themed Packs</a>:</strong> Dedicated modes for Cinema, Geography, History, Sports, Language, and Science.</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- Bottom CTA Bar -->
    <div class="mt-12 p-8 rounded-3xl bg-abyss-card border border-cyan-500/30 text-center not-prose space-y-4 shadow-xl">
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-white">Ready to Plunge Into the Abyss?</h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 max-w-md mx-auto">
        Join the global submarine expedition. Test your rarity knowledge on today's live 7 prompts.
      </p>
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3">
        <a href="/#game" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-cyan-400 to-blue-500 text-slate-950 font-black text-xs hover:scale-105 transition-all shadow-lg shadow-cyan-500/20">
          Play Daily Dive Now ⚓
        </a>
        <a href="/how-to-dive-7000m" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-white/5 hover:bg-white/10 text-white font-bold text-xs border border-white/10 transition-all">
          7,000m Strategy Guide
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
